From 17569eaeb1b01bc4749dfe455edfe8407e31cc49 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: terminills <tdeters@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 10:12:09 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 670/689] AROS: hardware VP9 decoding on the AMD VCN

Add a VP9 accelerator for VP9Decoder that builds VCN messages the way
radeonsi does on VCN 5.0 with a linear output: the dynamic (tier 2)
DPB, one 256B_D-swizzled DPB buffer per picture index tracked against
the eight reference slots, the probability table and segmentation data
in the message buffer, and the default probabilities seeded into the
context buffer. Profile 0 and profile 2 (decoded down to 8 bits) are
accepted.

amdgpu.hidd never reuses GART addresses, so buffers released by a
decoding session are kept and reused by later sessions instead of
being returned.

vcn_vp9_default.h is Mesa's ac_vcn_vp9_default.h (MIT).

Tested on the RX 9060 XT with bear-vp9.webm, bear-vp9-bt709.webm and
bear-vp9-odd-dimensions.webm: decoded through the VCN with correct
pictures.
